role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "460ba529-3a75-49f1-82a5-019394263c79", "content": "/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/.expo/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/xml2js/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/didyoumean/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/destroy/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/husky/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/expo-server/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/set-blocking/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/universalify/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/picocolors/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/react-native-url-polyfill/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/dunder-proto/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/wrappy/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/babel-plugin-react-compiler/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/eslint-scope/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/uc.micro/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/colorette/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/detective-es6/README.md\n/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/node_modules/natural-compare/README.md"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<tool_call>Read<arg_key>file_path</arg_key><arg_value>/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/BRIEF.md</arg_value></tool_call>", "reasoning_content": "Let me read the README.md, package.json, and explore the key directories to understand the project structure.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "a22b513b-2a3d-4b75-8bf7-6ba202c81c66", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/README.md\"}"}}, {"id": "70922c8e-a34c-464e-b3da-b8b8fa4655d2", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/package.json\"}"}}, {"id": "cd5c482a-3faf-4542-97fa-21f7eb3f8fc6", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/AGENTS.md\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "a22b513b-2a3d-4b75-8bf7-6ba202c81c66", "content": "1\t# \ud83c\udf93 EasyTutor v1.0: Infinite AI Learning Architecture\n2\t*The \"Professor\" that adapts to any student. From KICD High School to University Degree programs.*\n3\t\n4\t[![Expo SDK](https://img.shields.io/badge/Expo-SDK%2055-000000?style=for-the-badge&logo=expo&logoColor=white)](https://expo.dev)\n5\t[![AI Engine](https://img.shields.io/badge/AI-Claude%203.5%20Sonnet-6A4EEA?style=for-the-badge&logo=anthropic&logoColor=white)](https://anthropic.com)\n6\t[![Backend](https://img.shields.io/badge/Backend-Supabase-3ECF8E?style=for-the-badge&logo=supabase&logoColor=white)](https://supabase.com)\n7\t[![Styling](https://img.shields.io/badge/Styling-NativeWind-06B6D4?style=for-the-badge&logo=tailwindcss&logoColor=white)](https://tailwindcss.com)\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## \ud83c\udf1f The Vision\n12\t**EasyTutor** is not just an AI wrapper; it is a **multi-portal academic operating system**. \n13\tBuilt on a \"Universal Professor\" architecture, it detects whether a user is a **Kenyan High Schooler** (KICD syllabus), a **University Undergraduate** (Rigified Degree paths), or a **Self-Directed Learner** (Socratic Goal-driven), and dynamically re-architects its UI, system prompts, and curriculum generation logic to match.\n14\t\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f System Architecture: The \"Professor\" Model\n18\t\n19\tEasyTutor uses a tiered redirection and orchestration strategy:\n20\t\n21\t```mermaid\n22\tgraph TD\n23\t    A[User Sign-in] --> B{Onboarding Complete?}\n24\t    B -- No --> C[Multi-Card Selection Screen]\n25\t    B -- Yes --> D{Learning Mode?}\n26\t    \n27\t    C --> D\n28\t    \n29\t    D -- High School --> E[Portal: KICD Syllabus Explorer]\n30\t    D -- University --> F[Portal: Faculty Degree Browser]\n31\t    D -- Self-Directed --> G[Portal: Goal-Driven Mission Control]\n32\t    \n33\t    E --> H[Syllabus-Aligned Roadmaps]\n34\t    F --> I[Degree-Level AI Modules]\n35\t    G --> J[Socratic Study Paths]\n36\t    \n37\t    H & I & J --> K[Zod-Validated JSON AI API]\n38\t    K --> L[Shared Study Engine]\n39\t    L --> M[Cloud-Synced Progress Dashboard]\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\t---\n43\t\n44\t## \ud83d\ude80 Key Portal Features\n45\t\n46\t### \ud83c\uddf0\ud83c\uddea **Portal 1: High School (KICD-Aligned)**\n47\t- **Curriculum Native**: Pre-seeded with 12 Core KCSE subjects from Mathematics to Computer Studies.\n48\t- **Form-Level Content**: Topics are categorized by Form 1\u20134 to ensure exam-readiness.\n49\t- **KICD Context**: AI prompts are culturally and academically tuned for the Kenyan secondary system.\n50\t\n51\t### \ud83c\udf93 **Portal 2: University (Academic Rigor)**\n52\t- **Scholarly Depth**: Subjects include Medicine, Mechanical Engineering, Law, and Architecture.\n53\t- **Degree-Level AI**: System prompts shift from basic explanations to undergraduate-level academic logic.\n54\t- **Integrated Exams**: challenging 15-question simulators designed for degree mastery.\n55\t\n56\t### \ud83e\udded **Portal 3: Self-Directed (Explorer Mode)**\n57\t- **Goal Mission Control**: Enter any learning goal (e.g., \"Build a React-Native bridge\") and get an instant architected roadmap.\n58\t- **Socratic Guidance**: The AI focuses on questioning and deepening understanding rather than just lecturing.\n59\t\n60\t---\n61\t\n62\t## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f The Tech Stack (EasyTutor v1.0)\n63\t\n64\t- **Frontend**: **React Native v0.7x** with **Expo SDK 55**.\n65\t- **State Management**: **Zustand** with high-performance persistence using **AsyncStorage**.\n66\t- **Database Architecture**: **Supabase PostgreSQL** with strict Row-Level Security (RLS) for student data isolation.\n67\t- **AI Orchestration**: \n68\t  - **Primary**: Claude 3.5 Sonnet (via Anthropic SDK).\n69\t  - **Secondary**: Llama 3.1 8B (via Groq API) for high-speed fallback.\n70\t  - **Formatting**: **Zod Schemas** for 100% predictable AI JSON outputs.\n71\t\n72\t---\n73\t\n74\t## \ud83d\udcd0 Engineering Innovations\n75\t\n76\t### **1. AI Self-Healing & JSON Integrity**\n77\tTo eliminate hallucinations, the app implements a **Strict Validation-Retry Loop**. If the AI yields a malformed 7-day roadmap, the system automatically detects the schema error (via Zod) and re-executes the request with refined instructions, ensuring UI stability.\n78\t\n79\t### **2. Persona-Aware Prompt Injection**\n80\tEvery request to the AI is dynamically prepended with a portal-specific system prompt. The API layer \"knows\" the user's learning level and injects instructions to adapt the tone, depth, and cultural references in milliseconds.\n81\t\n82\t### **3. Reusable Educational Component Layer**\n83\tBuilt a specialized component library (`SubjectGrid`, `TopicList`, `QuizEngine`, `RoadmapView`) that shared between all portals, ensuring code-reuse while maintaining distinct visual branding for each learning level.\n84\t\n85\t---\n86\t\n87\t## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Installation & Setup\n88\t\n89\t1. **Clone & Install**:\n90\t   ```bash\n91\t   git clone https://github.com/dmuhoro/easytutor.git\n92\t   npm install --legacy-peer-deps\n93\t   ```\n94\t2. **Environment Configuration**:\n95\t   Create a `.env.local` and add:\n96\t   ```env\n97\t   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_url\n98\t   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_key\n99\t   EXPO_PUBLIC_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key\n100\t   ```\n101\t3. **Database Setup**:\n102\t   Run the SQL scripts in `/supabase/migrations` and `/supabase/*.sql` to seed the curriculum.\n103\t\n104\t4. **Launch**:\n105\t   ```bash\n106\t   npx expo start\n107\t   ```\n108\t\n109\t---\n110\t\n111\t## \ud83d\udcc4 License\n112\tMIT License. Created with \u2764\ufe0f by **Daniel Muhoro** (Project Orchestrator) & **Antigravity AI**.\n113\t"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "70922c8e-a34c-464e-b3da-b8b8fa4655d2", "content": "1\t{\n2\t  \"name\": \"easytutor\",\n3\t  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4\t  \"main\": \"expo-router/entry\",\n5\t  \"scripts\": {\n6\t    \"start\": \"expo start\",\n7\t    \"android\": \"expo run:android\",\n8\t    \"ios\": \"expo run:ios\",\n9\t    \"web\": \"expo start --web\",\n10\t    \"lint\": \"npx eslint . --ext .ts,.tsx || true\",\n11\t    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n12\t    \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n13\t    \"test:flows\": \"vitest run\",\n14\t    \"build\": \"npx expo export --platform web\",\n15\t    \"audit:full\": \"./scripts/full-audit.sh\",\n16\t    \"audit:governance\": \"node scripts/architecture/governance_audit.js\",\n17\t    \"dep:check\": \"madge --circular --extensions ts,tsx .\",\n18\t    \"dep:graph\": \"madge --image dependency-graph.png --extensions ts,tsx .\",\n19\t    \"doctor\": \"expo-doctor\"\n20\t  },\n21\t  \"dependencies\": {\n22\t    \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"^0.95.1\",\n23\t    \"@expo-google-fonts/dm-sans\": \"^0.4.2\",\n24\t    \"@expo-google-fonts/syne\": \"^0.4.2\",\n25\t    \"@expo/vector-icons\": \"^15.0.2\",\n26\t    \"@react-native-async-storage/async-storage\": \"^2.2.0\",\n27\t    \"@react-native-community/netinfo\": \"^11.5.2\",\n28\t    \"@supabase/supabase-js\": \"^2.100.0\",\n29\t    \"@types/react\": \"~19.2.10\",\n30\t    \"autoprefixer\": \"^10.4.27\",\n31\t    \"class-variance-authority\": \"^0.7.1\",\n32\t    \"clsx\": \"^2.1.1\",\n33\t    \"expo\": \"^55.0.23\",\n34\t    \"expo-blur\": \"~55.0.14\",\n35\t    \"expo-clipboard\": \"~55.0.13\",\n36\t    \"expo-constants\": \"~55.0.9\",\n37\t    \"expo-dev-client\": \"~55.0.28\",\n38\t    \"expo-font\": \"~55.0.4\",\n39\t    \"expo-haptics\": \"~55.0.14\",\n40\t    \"expo-linear-gradient\": \"~55.0.13\",\n41\t    \"expo-linking\": \"~55.0.14\",\n42\t    \"expo-router\": \"~55.0.13\",\n43\t    \"expo-secure-store\": \"~55.0.13\",\n44\t    \"expo-speech\": \"~55.0.13\",\n45\t    \"expo-splash-screen\": \"~55.0.19\",\n46\t    \"expo-status-bar\": \"~55.0.4\",\n47\t    \"expo-updates\": \"~55.0.21\",\n48\t    \"lucide-react-native\": \"^1.7.0\",\n49\t    \"nativewind\": \"^4.2.3\",\n50\t    \"postcss\": \"^8.5.8\",\n51\t    \"react\": \"19.2.0\",\n52\t    \"react-dom\": \"19.2.0\",\n53\t    \"react-native\": \"0.83.6\",\n54\t    \"react-native-markdown-display\": \"^7.0.2\",\n55\t    \"react-native-reanimated\": \"4.2.1\",\n56\t    \"react-native-safe-area-context\": \"~5.6.2\",\n57\t    \"react-native-screens\": \"~4.23.0\",\n58\t    \"react-native-svg\": \"15.15.3\",\n59\t    \"react-native-url-polyfill\": \"^2.0.0\",\n60\t    \"react-native-web\": \"^0.21.0\",\n61\t    \"react-native-worklets\": \"0.7.4\",\n62\t    \"tailwind-merge\": \"^3.5.0\",\n63\t    \"tailwindcss\": \"^3.4.19\",\n64\t    \"zod\": \"^4.3.6\",\n65\t    \"zustand\": \"^5.0.12\"\n66\t  },\n67\t  \"devDependencies\": {\n68\t    \"@react-native-community/cli\": \"latest\",\n69\t    \"@testing-library/react-native\": \"^13.3.3\",\n70\t    \"@types/react\": \"~19.2.10\",\n71\t    \"babel-preset-expo\": \"~55.0.8\",\n72\t    \"cross-fetch\": \"^3.2.0\",\n73\t    \"dependency-cruiser\": \"^17.4.0\",\n74\t    \"eslint\": \"^10.3.0\",\n75\t    \"husky\": \"^9.1.7\",\n76\t    \"lint-staged\": \"^16.4.0\",\n77\t    \"madge\": \"^8.0.0\",\n78\t    \"react-test-renderer\": \"^19.2.0\",\n79\t    \"typescript\": \"^5.9.3\",\n80\t    \"vitest\": \"^4.1.5\"\n81\t  },\n82\t  \"private\": true\n83\t}\n84\t"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "cd5c482a-3faf-4542-97fa-21f7eb3f8fc6", "content": "1\t# AI Agent Entry Point: Engineering OS v2\n2\t\n3\tThis repository is an AI-native engineering ecosystem. Every autonomous action MUST follow this protocol.\n4\t\n5\t## 1. Context Acquisition\n6\t- Read `ai-context/*` to understand the product and architecture.\n7\t- Read `AGENTS.md` to understand your operational role (see `/agents`).\n8\t\n9\t## 2. Pre-Implementation Validation\n10\t- Verify that a spec exists in `/specs/in-progress`.\n11\t- Check `ai-context/architecture.md` for non-negotiable invariants.\n12\t- Ensure no boundary violations (run `node scripts/architecture/validate_boundaries.js`).\n13\t\n14\t## 3. Scoped Execution\n15\t- Implement ONE unit at a time.\n16\t- Use defensive programming (timeouts, retries).\n17\t- Never modify stable logic unnecessarily.\n18\t\n19\t## 4. Post-Implementation Documentation\n20\t- Update `ai-context/current_state.md`.\n21\t- Record lessons in `/memory/lessons-learned.md`.\n22\t- Generate an audit trail in the spec file.\n23\t\n24\t## 5. Verification\n25\t- Run `node scripts/qa/qa_runner.js`.\n26\t- All steps MUST pass before completion.\n27\t\n28\t---\n29\t\n30\t# Deterministic Invariants\n31\t1. **Spec-Driven:** No code without a spec.\n32\t2. **Boundary-Safe:** No UI direct DB calls.\n33\t3. **Memory-Persistent:** Record every failure and lesson.\n34\t4. **Verified:** No completion without QA pass.\n35\t"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<tool_call>Bash<arg_key>command</arg_key><arg_value>ls -la /home/daniel-muhoro/workspace/projects/easytutor/src/</arg_value><arg_key>description</arg_key><arg_value>List src directory</arg_value></tool_call>", "reasoning_content": "Let me explore more of the codebase structure to understand the architecture better. I'll look at the key directories and files.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "975827a3-6b54-42f7-a443-68b188cb68f7", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"ls